Description: Show the lock screen and the full-screen demo after raising them on Linux
 LockWidget showed itself full screen and then called raiseWindow(this, true), which sets
 Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint on the shown window. Changing the window flags of a shown window makes Qt 5 hide it,
 so the lock screen (Lock) and the full-screen demo (Demo > share in full screen mode, a LockWidget too) never
 appeared on the students' computers, while the keyboard was disabled all the same. Show the widget normally
 first and full screen after raising it, as Veyon 4.8.0 does.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/veyon/veyon/commit/554bd2da1998258be109beedca2b25daf33f24b5
Bug: https://github.com/veyon/veyon/issues/824
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

--- a/core/src/LockWidget.cpp
+++ b/core/src/LockWidget.cpp
@@ -58,12 +58,20 @@
 
 	setWindowTitle( {} );
 
+#ifdef Q_OS_LINUX
+	show();
+#endif
 	move(leftMostScreen->geometry().topLeft());
+#ifndef Q_OS_LINUX
 	showFullScreen();
+#endif
 	windowHandle()->setScreen(leftMostScreen);
 	setFixedSize(leftMostScreen->virtualSize());
 
 	VeyonCore::platform().coreFunctions().raiseWindow(this, true);
+#ifdef Q_OS_LINUX
+	showFullScreen();
+#endif
 
 	setFocusPolicy( Qt::StrongFocus );
 	setFocus();
